WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.100
-I'm excited to talk to you.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.367
-I'm excited to
talk to you, as well.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.901
-Alright, good. I'm happy.
-Good to see you, man.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.601
It's been a long minute.
-It has been a little bit.

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.400
I think last time, you were here
with Anderson, right?

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.200
-Yes, sir, yep.
-Thanks for coming back.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.334
I know since your album --

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.133
the first album came out,

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.300
you've got two
Grammy nominations?

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.667
-Yes, sir, two.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.334
-Come on, bud.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:20.200
-Not too shabby. Not too bad.
-Not too bad.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.300
-Well, people knew --
People predicted that

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.901
you were going to be
this successful.

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:26.434
This is a photo we found
from your yearbook.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.400
Look at this.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.868
-"Most Likely to be Famous."

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:32.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:36.868
How did they predict this?

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.100
What were you like?
-You know, stars are born, man.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.434
-Oh, my gosh. Oh, my gosh.
-You know.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.734
But I used to always drop,
you know,

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.300
mix tapes very --
when I was younger.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.567
I dropped my first mix tape
when I was 15 years old.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.100
I used to always perform at,
like, the school talent shows.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.434
Like, I was a rapper.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.501
Like -- And it's not cool
being an artist

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:56.200
before you're on Jimmy Fallon's
couch, you know?

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.601
-No. Who did
you want to be like?

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:58.834
Who were your idols?

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:02.033
-You know, Kanye West
was a big idol of mine.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.067
Kendrick Lamar.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.400
-Yeah.
-Nas. Jay-Z.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.601
-Yeah. Yeah, a couple -- Yeah.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.434
-You might have heard of them.
-Yeah, a couple. Yeah, exactly.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:12.801
What were your rhymes like
when you were little?

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:16.334
How little were you when you
were starting to write songs?

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.300
-I think my first rhyme, I might
have been like 4 to 5 years old,

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.367
and it was like --

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.868
-5 years old?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.000
I've been doing this for
a minute.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.200
I've been doing this
for a minute.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.300
-What would those be --
What would you be --

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.567
-It was like --
Something dumb like,

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:31.067
"Reese's Puffs and cuffs
with earmuffs.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.100
Look, man, I'm too tough.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.200
'Cause I'm a survivor.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.367
Y'all burn like hot lava."
You know?

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.434
-Thanks for doing that.
I loved that.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:40.868
-Super G-rated. Super G-rated.

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.701
-Super G-rated.
Absolutely, yeah.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:45.834
Well, not only are you one of
the biggest out there now

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.000
and working with everybody --

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.634
I mean, Dre, H.E.R.,
Eminem, Lil Wayne --

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.334
but you also have
your own record label.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:55.400
-Yeah.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.734
-Talk about Hi Level.
What is this?

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:59.200
-Yeah, so, Hi Level --
Y'all can clap for that.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.868
-Yeah, absolutely.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's a big deal.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.667
-Yeah, thank you.
Appreciate that.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.734
But, you know, Hi Level -- it's
more than just a record label.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.167
It's really a mantra,
a way of life, you know?

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:11.300
And I sort of had this epiphany,
if you will,

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.100
right through
the middle of a pandemic.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.868
It's a frame of mind
I always like to have.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.667
Like, everything I do, I must do
it at the highest level,

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.367
at a high level, the highest
level of my capability.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.100
So that's where Hi Level
came from.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.767
-When you go back home,
does your mom

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:25.834
treat you like a big deal?

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.334
I mean, does the hometown
go nuts or no?

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.501
Are you still just Cordae?

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:31.934
-you know, she's not that
impressed, to be honest.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.200
-Yeah, that's what moms do.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.367
They've got to keep you back
down at this level.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.634
-For sure.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:38.100
I go back home, it's
I've got to wash the dishes,

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.501
got to, you know, mow the lawn.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:40.801
For real. This is a real thing.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:44.234
And I think that's her way of
like, "Hold on, now.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.968
Don't have too much
dip on your chip, now."

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.667
You know? So...

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.100
-"Don't have too much
dip on your chip."

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.267
I love that.

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.968
This Friday,
the new album is coming out.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:01.400
Are you ready?
Everybody excited for it?

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.267
-You know, I just reached that
point to where true faith

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:08.400
is just having, you know,
no fear in the unknown,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.434
and that's where
I'm at right now.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:10.601
So I feel really good.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.300
I say all that to say,
I feel really good.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.801
-This is --
It comes out this Friday.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.567
"From A Bird's Eye View"
is the --

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.701
I love the album cover
and the artwork, by the way.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.934
Where did it -- [ Laughs ]

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:25.767
Where did it come from, the
idea, "From A Bird's Eye View"?

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:27.000
What does it mean?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.033
-It means to see things
from outside of yourself.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.267
You know, as human beings,

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:33.267
we tend to all have, like,
main-character syndrome.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:35.200
But -- Seriously, though.
-Yeah.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.767
-But it's to see things from
a more zoomed-out lens.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.334
You know, that's like me and you
can in an argument on TV --

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:41.501
Hopefully not, right? --

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:42.868
But we can get
in an argument here,

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.734
and I can leave here like,
"Oh, man, you know, Jimmy --

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:46.601
he is kind of,
like, not a nice guy,"

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.400
but to see things from a
bird's-eye view, it's like,

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.200
"Oh, I can understand
how I was wrong in this way."

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.601
So to see things
from a wider lens,

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:53.968
a more broader perspective.

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:55.701
-Disagree, but, yeah,
we all have different opinions.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:56.801
Well, that's why we're here.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:57.934
I mean,
we're all different, right?

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.000
-Absolutely.
-Yeah.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.167
-One way or another.

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:01.534
-What are you performing
for us tonight?

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:02.968
-I'm going to
perform a medley --

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:06.100
"Sinister" and song that's not
quite out yet, "Chronicles."

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.734
-That's what I'm talking about.
-Come on.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:10.033
-Cordae,
"From A Bird's Eye View"

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.701
is available this Friday.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.467
Cordae's performing for us
after the break.

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.467
Come on back.

